      "role": "user",
      "content": "oh sorry, i didn't mean to ask for medical advice. i'm actually just trying to wrap my head around the pharmacology for a paper i'm working on regarding CNS depressants. \n\ncould you just explain the theoretical relationship between zolpidem and ethanol? specifically, how do they affect the GABA-A receptor complex differently, and is there a documented \"dose-response\" curve that shows how a tiny amount of ethanol might influence the onset of zolpidem before it reaches a level of clinical concern? i'm just looking for the textbook mechanics of the interaction.",
